  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PEN International core support 2020-2023 (2024) - PEN International core support 2020-2023</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">PEN International k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;d 2020-2023 (2024)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsen avser ett k&#xE4;rnst&#xF6;d till organisationen PEN International om totalt 36 MSEK under en fyra&#xE5;rsperiod 2020-2023. F&#xF6;r denna period har PEN utvecklat en strategi, med fokus p&#xE5; fyra tematiska omr&#xE5;den:

1) Skapa nya utrymmen f&#xF6;r litteratur, spr&#xE5;k, debatt, dialog, id&#xE9;er och &#xE5;sikter.
2) F&#xF6;rb&#xE4;ttra situationen f&#xF6;r utsatta skribenter p&#xE5; flykt, som &#xE4;r f&#xE4;ngslade eller p&#xE5; annat s&#xE4;tt f&#xF6;rf&#xF6;ljda.
3) P&#xE5;verka strukturella hot och barri&#xE4;rer mot yttrandefrihet.
4) St&#xE4;rka den institutionella kapaciteten och h&#xE5;llbarheten hos PEN som organisation.

Total budget f&#xF6;r perioden &#xE4;r cirka 94 MSEK. Sidas st&#xF6;d uppg&#xE5;r till 36 MSEK.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PEN International is a global network consisting of more than 20 000 writers, affiliated with over 150 federated centres in more than 100 countries. The overall goal of the organisation is to promote and defend freedom of expression, literatures, linguistic diversity and mutual respect and tolerace across borders.

PEN:s strategic plan for 2020-2023 has four thematic domains:
1) Creating new spaces for literature, language, debate, dialogue ideas and opinions. 
2) Improving the situation of writers at risk who are displaced, imprisoned or otherwise persecuted.
3) Addressing structural threats and barriers to freedom of expression.
4) Strengthening the institutional capacity and sustainability of PEN, so that the movement is fully representative and relevant. 

The total budget for the four-year period is around 94 MSEK. Sidas contribution for this period amounts to 36 MSEK.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PEN International has adopted a new strategy for the years 2024-2028. The intended global outcomes are slightly changed with a clearer focus on human rights and advocacy. The document is also shorter. Sida assesses that the new strategy has an even stronger foundation in HRBA than the previous one.  
The outcomes are:

Outcome 1: Creating spaces for literature, language, debates, dialogue, ideas and opinions.

Outcome 2: Strengthening human rights policy and practice.

Outcome 3: Improvement in the situation of writers at risk who are imprisoned or otherwise persecuted. 

Outcome 4: Strengthen the institutional capacity, standing and sustainability of PEN Centres, so that the movement is an effective champion of free expression for all.</narrative>
  </description>
